Three steps:

1. Find the right module. It matches the CVE from stage 2 and
   it's the *exploit*, not the detector.
     grep -l "CVE-2018-1000861" modules/*
     # two hits. Read both headers. Pick the one that says exploit.

2. Pick a payload from that module's COMPATIBLE PAYLOADS list.
   Check payloads/ to make sure the architecture matches the
   target (re-read your stage 1 scan — kernel reports i686).

3. Assemble RHOST, RPORT, TARGETURI from earlier stages. Fire.
